        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 85-year-old female patient, admitted on 22/01/2010 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gases revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. Her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged on 23/01/2010 with oral steroids and inhaled bronchodilators. Please ensure close follow-up and review of her maintenance inhaler therapy. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
